  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating the skewness of each lottery and preferring the one that is more right-skewed (i.e., higher concentration of probability on unfavorable outcomes). Lottery B is more right-skewed and would be preferred by the reason. However, the individual in the verbal report focuses only on minimizing the probability of a loss, which is a different criterion. Right-skewness preference would favor the lottery with higher probability of loss (if that loss is smaller or less severe), but the individual instead seeks to avoid any loss with higher priority on lower loss probability. The information considered by the individual (loss probability) differs from the information required for skewness (distribution of favorable vs. unfavorable outcomes and their imbalance). Furthermore, the justification (minimizing chance of loss) contradicts the logic of preferring more right-skewed lotteries, which typically have higher loss probabilities. Therefore, there is no alignment between the reason’s basis and the individual’s deliberation.",
